es","target_id":"244b-4163-df5d-4990"},{"link_uuid":"87c04216-1a21-4d44-886a-07147b139168","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"83d8-a708-c69e-41be"},{"link_uuid":"3f846d3f-e010-4ec2-88fa-96903b79f1d9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"920e-79d9-6a5e-4de5"},{"link_uuid":"28a2fec5-7dac-4ec5-b4b1-21e6f8e187f2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3794-3a84-3a44-41f7"},{"link_uuid":"fd9e2419-a5fd-481d-aac2-acdbd373b392","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5394-5578-ee7c-493b"},{"link_uuid":"453e4ce8-2973-45f2-bfd4-6a8ea3aef6c6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"37ea-35ab-fd93-4d5b"},{"link_uuid":"48535317-6840-4725-9b70-22f3b99d0040","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c9b8-38b2-0ec0-4c15"},{"link_uuid":"621ca204-142c-40c6-ba64-5bac9d56c071","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"64fb-a7c7-bda7-4e2a"},{"link_uuid":"d3559e65-2886-46c3-b91c-eea2e9c22863","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8606-6030-1b41-4d9a"},{"link_uuid":"1f4ff75c-b277-4212-b247-c65192226ca5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d85f-5f5a-ee80-4bbc"},{"link_uuid":"7f5fbdb5-e1f6-4eb8-b812-bf7d63f3c298","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"506a-cb6d-23d5-4d3f"},{"link_uuid":"d9131f4e-69cc-45d5-bd53-ce27f5d73450","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7b97-0033-3ea5-4aef"},{"link_uuid":"3e743d6c-d11d-4cc0-a0cd-b3ae0dd2b079","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ffe5-87ef-0351-495b"},{"link_uuid":"b658fc90-b6aa-42cf-bff7-6adddb097f27","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b2b9-c03f-79d0-473d"},{"link_uuid":"c1ff4f6d-3b9e-41b7-bce4-691d9532c0ca","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e4e6-8d0a-4c37-4e25"},{"link_uuid":"3582516b-4bfa-40cc-892b-89ee6b7a851e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0a2f-a198-877a-432d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen reusable and operational workflow files contain explanatory comments that mix current contracts with repetition, narration, or history. Scope was revalidated on `origin/main@d6669496cae4`, including the Terraform-config-inspect canary appended to `_optionality.yml`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only allowlisted standalone explanatory comments and adjacent blank lines. Keep current non-obvious rationale, security boundaries, failure semantics, portability constraints, and operator-visible contracts. Preserve all workflow data, embedded shell, expressions, permissions, triggers, action pins, assertions, user-facing output, and directives byte-for-byte.\n\nPreserve these behavior-bearing directive lines exactly:\n- `_artifact-probe.yml`: both `shellcheck disable=SC1091` lines.\n- `_mutation.yml` and `gerrit-verify.yaml`: all four `predates-gate-ok` markers.\n- `gerrit-verify.yaml`, `prompt-eval.yml`, and `_optionality.yml`: all five complete `mechanism-ok: ci_gate` markers, including the three Terraform-canary markers.\n\n## Scope\n- `_artifact-probe.yml` — Preserve secret-free exact-patchset checkout, sdist-first build, baked-commit/metadata checks, installed archive probes, schema/import walk, and shellcheck directives.\n- `_build-and-test.yml` — Preserve secret-free exact checkout; online-token versus portable local lint; pre-commit skips; old-patchset guards; ownership-routed dependency advisories; enforced sandbox proof; Linux/macOS, coverage, extras, and Node lanes; browser opt-out record; patchset timeout; integration isolation; Gerrit report coverage; trusted-main docs restore; and generated/parity/security gates.\n- `_eval-discipline.yml` — Preserve both callers, secret/model-free exact-patchset evaluation, named offline subset, and 300-second thread bound.\n- `_mutation.yml` — Preserve changed/all shard selection, empty-selection skip, 30-minute shards, always-uploaded evidence, hosted-Ubuntu namespace waiver, and exact predates marker.\n- `_optionality.yml` — Preserve fork-safe checkout; clean no-extra wheel and heavy-dependency absence; old-patchset guards; no-agents degradation; isolated per-extra environments, union resolution, absolute interpreters, and aggregated failure. Also condense the shell-comment block before the Terraform canary's if-present guard while preserving the main-definition/patchset-tree mismatch rationale, early skip before installs, all canary workflow data, the pinned upstream binary, opt-in environment, and three exact mechanism markers.\n- `codeql.yml` — Preserve schedule/manual-only triggering, six-hour staggering, cancellation, Python/JavaScript matrix, path config, read-only permissions with job-local security-event write, and intentional major action tags.\n- `compact-sweep.yml` — Preserve out-of-band single flight; full-history ticket merge; harmless 60-minute bound; sweep-only write; optional signing; dry-run/limit inputs; exit-2 warning versus exit-1 failure; no-pipe capture; always-written summary; and operation-linked no-CI fallback. It publishes no metrics.\n- `dependency-advisory-canary.yml` — Preserve daily/manual dry-run, single flight, writable full-history store, optional signing, deduplicated lifecycle/comment cap, release-only blocking, merge-not-rebase retry flush, and visible red result. The audit step remains `continue-on-error`; the alert step must fail closed.\n- `external-integration.yml` — Preserve manual/weekly billable boundary; provider isolation and loud missing/all-skip failure; committed overlays; Bedrock-only OIDC and regions; complementary partitions, per-test timeouts, usage evidence; Langfuse/Jira teardown; scoped S3 and Jira Cloud cleanup; and Linux/macOS Pandoc replay.\n- `gerrit-verify.yaml` — Preserve authoritative patchset identity; exact checkout; trusted-main classifier/normalizer/vote code; secret confinement; exclusive routing; complete `vote.needs`; fail-closed conclusions; closed-change race handling; non-voting observability; and exact markers.\n- `jira-dc-capability-map.yml` — Preserve manual amd64 authoring, pinned harness, required Anthropic access, bounded agent run, read-only repository store, teardown, and artifact.\n- `jira-dc-epic-link-probe.yml` — Preserve the manual stdlib/four-call disposable-Jira probe, no LLM or repository mutation, teardown, and artifact.\n- `jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml` — Preserve mirror-first/Gerrit-fallback exact fetch/SHA verification; mismatch/all-skip failure; DC extra; isolated no-remotes suite; teardown; additive non-Verified role; and summary/log evidence.\n- `jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml` — Preserve manual Anthropic investigation, shared harness, direct-provider overlay, read-only repository store, bounded run, evidence upload, and teardown.\n- `mirror-guard.yml` — Preserve 15-minute/manual replication checks, multiple samples, public/default-token reads, cancellation, and exclusion of admin-only ruleset drift.\n- `optionality.yml` — Preserve mirror caller filters, pull requests, manual/staggered health, read-only/no-vote posture, and branch-head reusable invocation.\n- `prompt-eval.yml` — Preserve offline branch/PR/manual evaluation; advisory same-repo changed-rubric evaluation; canonical weekly/manual live evaluation; sequential cases, cap 12, provider dollar caps, summaries/artifacts, concurrency, and exact marker.\n- `reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` — Preserve rollback input, cadence/window, single flight, write/read permissions, full-history store, optional signing, consecutive-red lifecycle, binding fsck, synchronous merge-not-rebase push, dry-run, and terminal stale red.\n\nPaths are relative to `.github/workflows/`. Consumers are GitHub Actions, repository policy tests, bridge/runtime code, and operators.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only allowlisted standalone comments or adjacent blank lines change in the 18 paths; workflow data, embedded shell, and exact directives remain byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer has a concrete before/final PASS citation in a leaf-linked TSV authored by a non-author reviewer.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and records `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] Comment-only and directive guards, focused workflow tests, path-scoped diff checks, and no-timeout worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded deterministic commands. The independent TSV, not exact prose retention, is authoritative for concision and semantic preservation.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_artifact-probe.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_eval-discipline.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_mutation.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/codeql.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/external-integration.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-epic-link-probe.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"pa